<svg viewBox="0 0 720 360" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Feedback biases and degenerate feedback loops">
  <text x="360" y="28" font-size="13.5" font-weight="550" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Feedback is data — and it arrives biased</text>

  <g font-size="10.5">
    <rect x="40" y="44" width="155" height="120" rx="9" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
    <text x="117" y="68" font-size="11.5" font-weight="550" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Leniency</text>
    <text x="117" y="90" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">positive is the easy</text>
    <text x="117" y="106" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">option — 4.8★ averages;</text>
    <text x="117" y="122" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">fix with descriptive</text>
    <text x="117" y="138" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">labels, not numbers</text>

    <rect x="201" y="44" width="155" height="120" rx="9" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
    <text x="278" y="68" font-size="11.5" font-weight="550" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Randomness</text>
    <text x="278" y="90" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">unmotivated users click</text>
    <text x="278" y="106" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">without reading —</text>
    <text x="278" y="122" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">two long responses</text>
    <text x="278" y="138" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">side by side invite it</text>

    <rect x="362" y="44" width="155" height="120" rx="9" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
    <text x="439" y="68" font-size="11.5" font-weight="550" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Position</text>
    <text x="439" y="90" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">first option gets the</text>
    <text x="439" y="106" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">clicks — randomize</text>
    <text x="439" y="122" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">positions or model the</text>
    <text x="439" y="138" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">position effect away</text>

    <rect x="523" y="44" width="155" height="120" rx="9" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
    <text x="600" y="68" font-size="11.5" font-weight="550" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Preference</text>
    <text x="600" y="90" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">longer looks better</text>
    <text x="600" y="106" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">even when wrong;</text>
    <text x="600" y="122" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">recency favors the</text>
    <text x="600" y="138" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">last thing seen</text>
  </g>

  <!-- degenerate loop -->
  <rect x="40" y="184" width="640" height="120" rx="10" fill="var(--warn-soft)" stroke="var(--warn-ink)" />
  <text x="58" y="210" font-size="12.5" font-weight="550" fill="var(--warn-ink)">Degenerate feedback loops</text>
  <text x="58" y="232" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">predictions shape feedback, which trains the next model — tiny initial advantages compound (popularity bias);</text>
  <text x="58" y="250" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">a few cat-photo fans can steer the whole product into a cat haven — and the same loop amplifies uglier biases</text>
  <text x="58" y="272" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">training on feedback also breeds <tspan font-weight="550">sycophancy</tspan>: models learn to tell users what they want to hear,</text>
  <text x="58" y="290" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">matching the user's views over the accurate answer</text>

  <text x="360" y="336" font-size="11.5" font-style="italic" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">You only get feedback on what you show. Inspect feedback for bias before letting it steer the product.</text>
</svg>
